{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01M3rKxrVotje1Le2Cxa1Y7R","type":"tool_result","content":"0\tid: srd056-cp\n1\ttitle: \"cmd/cp: Copy Files and Directories\"\n2\t\n3\tproblem: |\n4\t  cp is a fundamental file operation utility used for duplicating files and directory\n5\t  trees. The macOS BSD cp differs from GNU cp in attribute preservation semantics,\n6\t  reflink support, and sparse file handling. The Go implementation must match the\n7\t  Homebrew GNU reference binary (gcp, installed by coreutils) on exit codes and\n8\t  observable file system state for all supported flag combinations, verified by\n9\t  differential testing via pkg/testutils.\n10\t\n11\tgoals:\n12\t  - G1: Copy files and directories with configurable attribute preservation.\n13\t  - G2: Support recursive directory copying with symlink and special file handling.\n14\t  - G3: Support interactive, force, and no-clobber modes for destination conflict resolution.\n15\t  - G4: Verify functional parity against gcp via differential testing.\n16\t\n17\trequirements:\n18\t  R1:\n19\t    title: Basic file copying\n20\t    items:\n21\t      - R1.1:\n22\t          text: \"When given SOURCE DEST, must copy SOURCE to DEST. When given multiple SOURCE arguments and a DEST directory, must copy each SOURCE into DEST.\"\n23\t      - R1.2:\n24\t          text: \"-i or --interactive must prompt before overwriting an existing destination file.\"\n25\t      - R1.3:\n26\t          text: \"-f or --force must remove an existing destination file if it cannot be opened for writing, then retry the copy.\"\n27\t      - R1.4:\n28\t          text: \"-n or --no-clobber must not overwrite an existing destination file. When combined with -i, -n takes precedence.\"\n29\t\n30\t  R2:\n31\t    title: Recursive copying and symlinks\n32\t    items:\n33\t      - R2.1:\n34\t          text: \"-r or -R or --recursive must copy directories recursively, preserving the directory structure.\"\n35\t      - R2.2:\n36\t          text: \"Without -r, must refuse to copy a directory and print an error to stderr.\"\n37\t      - R2.3:\n38\t          text: \"-L or --dereference must follow symlinks in SOURCE, copying the file they point to.\"\n39\t      - R2.4:\n40\t          text: \"-P or --no-dereference must preserve symlinks, copying them as symlinks rather than following them. This is the default with -r.\"\n41\t\n42\t  R3:\n43\t    title: Attribute preservation\n44\t    items:\n45\t      - R3.1:\n46\t          text: \"-p or --preserve=mode,ownership,timestamps must preserve file mode, ownership, and modification timestamps on the copy.\"\n47\t      - R3.2:\n48\t          text: \"-a or --archive is equivalent to -dR --preserve=all. It preserves all attributes and copies recursively without following symlinks.\"\n49\t      - R3.3:\n50\t          text: \"--preserve=ATTR_LIST must accept a comma-separated list of attributes to preserve. Supported attributes are mode, ownership, timestamps, and links.\"\n51\t      - R3.4:\n52\t          text: \"-v or --verbose must print the name of each file as it is copied.\"\n53\t\n54\t  R4:\n55\t    title: Exit codes and differential testing\n56\t    items:\n57\t      - R4.1:\n58\t          text: Must exit 0 when all files are copied successfully.\n59\t      - R4.2:\n60\t          text: Must exit 1 when any copy operation fails (permission denied, source not found, destination is a directory without -r).\n61\t      - R4.3:\n62\t          text: \"-t DIRECTORY or --target-directory=DIRECTORY must copy all SOURCE arguments into DIRECTORY.\"\n63\t      - R4.4:\n64\t          text: \"Differential tests must compare exit codes and resulting file system state between the Go binary and the reference binary via pkg/testutils. Tests must cover: single file copy, multi-file copy into directory, -r recursive, -i interactive (via stdin), -f force, -n no-clobber, -p preserve, -a archive, -v verbose, symlink handling, and error cases.\"\n65\t\n66\tnon_goals:\n67\t  - \"cmd/cp does not implement --reflink (copy-on-write clones). Reflink support is filesystem-dependent and not available on all platforms.\"\n68\t  - cmd/cp does not implement --sparse (sparse file detection and reproduction).\n69\t  - cmd/cp does not implement -u (copy only when source is newer).\n70\t  - cmd/cp does not implement --backup (make backups of existing destination files).\n71\t  - cmd/cp does not implement SELinux context preservation (--context).\n72\t\n73\tacceptance_criteria:\n74\t  - id: AC1\n75\t    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/cp file1.txt file2.txt creates an identical copy, matching gcp.\"\n76\t    traces:\n77\t      - R1.1\n78\t      - R1.2\n79\t      - R1.3\n80\t      - R1.4\n81\t  - id: AC2\n82\t    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/cp -r dir1/ dir2/ recursively copies the directory tree, matching gcp.\"\n83\t    traces:\n84\t      - R2.1\n85\t      - R2.2\n86\t      - R2.4\n87\t      - R4.2\n88\t      - R4.4\n89\t  - id: AC3\n90\t    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/cp -p file1.txt file2.txt preserves mode and timestamps, matching gcp.\"\n91\t    traces:\n92\t      - R3.1\n93\t      - R4.4\n94\t  - id: AC4\n95\t    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/cp -n existing.txt target.txt does not overwrite target, matching gcp.\"\n96\t    traces:\n97\t      - R1.4\n98\t      - R4.4\n99\t  - id: AC5\n100\t    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/cp nonexistent.txt target.txt exits 1 with error on stderr, matching gcp.\"\n101\t    traces:\n102\t      - R2.2\n103\t      - R4.1\n104\t      - R4.2\n105\t      - R4.4\n106\t  - id: AC6\n107\t    criterion: \"Differential test against gcp passes for all flag combinations listed in R4.4.\"\n108\t    traces:\n109\t      - R4.4\n110\t  - id: AC7\n111\t    criterion: \"cmd/cp compiles with no warnings under golangci-lint.\"\n112\t    traces:\n113\t      - R1.1\n114\t      - R1.2\n115\t      - R1.3\n116\t      - R1.4\n117\t      - R2.1\n118\t      - R2.2\n119\t      - R2.3\n120\t      - R2.4\n121\t      - R3.1\n122\t      - R3.2\n123\t      - R3.3\n124\t      - R3.4\n125\t      - R4.1\n126\t      - R4.2\n127\t      - R4.3\n128\t      - R4.4\n129\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1273c734-52b1-41f4-bc95-2c61f3011a70","uuid":"6b9fbae4-5650-45fa-9af6-7863b6adb28a","timestamp":"2026-05-21T00:32:55.744Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5394/docs/specs/software-requirements/srd056-cp.yaml","content":"id: srd056-cp\ntitle: \"cmd/cp: Copy Files and Directories\"\n\nproblem: |\n  cp is a fundamental file operation utility used for duplicating files and directory\n  trees. The macOS BSD cp differs from GNU cp in attribute preservation semantics,\n  reflink support, and sparse file handling. The Go implementation must match the\n  Homebrew GNU reference binary (gcp, installed by coreutils) on exit codes and\n  observable file system state for all supported flag combinations, verified by\n  differential testing via pkg/testutils.\n\ngoals:\n  - G1: Copy files and directories with configurable attribute preservation.\n  - G2: Support recursive directory copying with symlink and special file handling.\n  - G3: Support interactive, force, and no-clobber modes for destination conflict resolution.\n  - G4: Verify functional parity against gcp via differential testing.\n\nrequirements:\n  R1:\n    title: Basic file copying\n    items:\n      - R1.1:\n          text: \"When given SOURCE DEST, must copy SOURCE to DEST. When given multiple SOURCE arguments and a DEST directory, must copy each SOURCE into DEST.\"\n      - R1.2:\n          text: \"-i or --interactive must prompt before overwriting an existing destination file.\"\n      - R1.3:\n          text: \"-f or --force must remove an existing destination file if it cannot be opened for writing, then retry the copy.\"\n      - R1.4:\n          text: \"-n or --no-clobber must not overwrite an existing destination file. When combined with -i, -n takes precedence.\"\n\n  R2:\n    title: Recursive copying and symlinks\n    items:\n      - R2.1:\n          text: \"-r or -R or --recursive must copy directories recursively, preserving the directory structure.\"\n      - R2.2:\n          text: \"Without -r, must refuse to copy a directory and print an error to stderr.\"\n      - R2.3:\n          text: \"-L or --dereference must follow symlinks in SOURCE, copying the file they point to.\"\n      - R2.4:\n          text: \"-P or --no-dereference must preserve symlinks, copying them as symlinks rather than following them. This is the default with -r.\"\n\n  R3:\n    title: Attribute preservation\n    items:\n      - R3.1:\n          text: \"-p or --preserve=mode,ownership,timestamps must preserve file mode, ownership, and modification timestamps on the copy.\"\n      - R3.2:\n          text: \"-a or --archive is equivalent to -dR --preserve=all. It preserves all attributes and copies recursively without following symlinks.\"\n      - R3.3:\n          text: \"--preserve=ATTR_LIST must accept a comma-separated list of attributes to preserve. Supported attributes are mode, ownership, timestamps, and links.\"\n      - R3.4:\n          text: \"-v or --verbose must print the name of each file as it is copied.\"\n\n  R4:\n    title: Exit codes and differential testing\n    items:\n      - R4.1:\n          text: Must exit 0 when all files are copied successfully.\n      - R4.2:\n          text: Must exit 1 when any copy operation fails (permission denied, source not found, destination is a directory without -r).\n      - R4.3:\n          text: \"-t DIRECTORY or --target-directory=DIRECTORY must copy all SOURCE arguments into DIRECTORY.\"\n      - R4.4:\n          text: \"Differential tests must compare exit codes and resulting file system state between the Go binary and the reference binary via pkg/testutils. Tests must cover: single file copy, multi-file copy into directory, -r recursive, -i interactive (via stdin), -f force, -n no-clobber, -p preserve, -a archive, -v verbose, symlink handling, and error cases.\"\n\nnon_goals:\n  - \"cmd/cp does not implement --reflink (copy-on-write clones). Reflink support is filesystem-dependent and not available on all platforms.\"\n  - cmd/cp does not implement --sparse (sparse file detection and reproduction).\n  - cmd/cp does not implement -u (copy only when source is newer).\n  - cmd/cp does not implement --backup (make backups of existing destination files).\n  - cmd/cp does not implement SELinux context preservation (--context).\n\nacceptance_criteria:\n  - id: AC1\n    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/cp file1.txt file2.txt creates an identical copy, matching gcp.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R1.2\n      - R1.3\n      - R1.4\n  - id: AC2\n    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/cp -r dir1/ dir2/ recursively copies the directory tree, matching gcp.\"\n    traces:\n      - R2.1\n      - R2.2\n      - R2.4\n      - R4.2\n      - R4.4\n  - id: AC3\n    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/cp -p file1.txt file2.txt preserves mode and timestamps, matching gcp.\"\n    traces:\n      - R3.1\n      - R4.4\n  - id: AC4\n    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/cp -n existing.txt target.txt does not overwrite target, matching gcp.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.4\n      - R4.4\n  - id: AC5\n    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/cp nonexistent.txt target.txt exits 1 with error on stderr, matching gcp.\"\n    traces:\n      - R2.2\n      - R4.1\n      - R4.2\n      - R4.4\n  - id: AC6\n    criterion: \"Differential test against gcp passes for all flag combinations listed in R4.4.\"\n    traces:\n      - R4.4\n  - id: AC7\n    criterion: \"cmd/cp compiles with no warnings under golangci-lint.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R1.2\n      - R1.3\n      - R1.4\n      - R2.1\n      - R2.2\n      - R2.3\n      - R2.4\n      - R3.1\n      - R3.2\n      - R3.3\n      - R3.4\n      - R4.1\n      - R4.2\n      - R4.3\n      - R4.4\n","numLines":130,"startLine":0,"totalLines":130}}}
